      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This issue occurs frequently for my friends' world, which normally contains about 40+ people and where is used for about 1 hour, or more.\nFrom my sight, despite actual movements of people, they are freezed but a bit shaking per a few frames.\nDuring this effect, there're tons of flowing logs (non-stop!) about `failed to adjust pose` for everybody in the world.\nAt the beginning of the phenomena, the logs tell that Ping/Delay/ShortBy values are about 0.2/0.6/0.6 respectively.\nThose values increases as time elapsed, in fact it eventually became about 170/170/440 respectively after 10 minutes.\nI hope this info to be useful. This problem is critical for some communities, contains us.\n\nNote: my env is i7-4790, GeForce GTX 980, 16.0GB. Some friends have reported that improving PC specs helped to resolve the issue.\n\nAdditional Note: Changing avatar from humanoid to generic looks causing a `failed to adjust pose` log per second. The entire problem lies another point I think.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
